y fries, Central: (205 \u00d7 45) / 450 = 20.50\n- Curly fries, West: (205 \u00d7 65) / 450 = 29.17\n\n- Steak fries, Northeast: (80 \u00d7 190) / 450 = 32.22\n- Steak fries, South: (80 \u00d7 150) / 450 = 26.67\n- Steak fries, Central: (80 \u00d7 45) / 450 = 8.00\n- Steak fries, West: (80 \u00d7 65) / 450 = 11.78\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the chi-square test statistic.**\n\u03c7\u00b2 = \u03a3 [(O\u1d62\u2c7c - E\u1d62\u2c7c)\u00b2 / E\u1d62\u2c7c]\n\nCalculate for each cell:\n\n- Skinny fries, Northeast: (70 - 31.17)\u00b2 / 31.17 = (38.83)\u00b2 / 31.17 \u2248 1508.47 / 31.17 \u2248 48.38\n- Skinny fries, South: (50 - 55.00)\u00b2 / 55.00 = (-5.00)\u00b2 / 55.00 = 25 / 55 \u2248 0.45\n- Skinny fries, Central: (20 - 16.50)\u00b2 / 16.50 = (3.5)\u00b2 / 16.50 = 12.25 / 16.50 \u2248 0.74\n- Skinny fries, West: (25 - 23.44)\u00b2 / 23.44 = (1.56)\u00b2 / 23.44 \u2248 2.43 / 23.44 \u2248 0.10\n\n- Curly fries, Northeast: (100 - 85.56)\u00b2 / 85.56 = (14.44)\u00b2 / 85.56 \u2248 208.51 / 85.56 \u2248 2.44\n- Curly fries, South: (60 - 68.33)\u00b2 / 68.33 = (-8.33)\u00b2 / 68.33 \u2248 69.44 / 68.33 \u2248 1.02\n- Curly fries, Central: (15 - 20.50)\u00b2 / 20.50 = (-5.5)\u00b2 / 20.50 = 30.25 / 20.50 \u2248 1.48\n- Curly fries, West: (30 - 29.17)\u00b2 / 29.17 = (0.83)\u00b2 / 29.17 \u2248 0.69 / 29.17 \u2248 0.02\n\n- Steak fries, Northeast: (20 - 32.22)\u00b2 / 32.22 = (-12.22)\u00b2 / 32.22 \u2248 149.33 / 32.22 \u2248 4.64\n- Steak fries, South: (40 - 26.67)\u00b2 / 26.67 = (13.33)\u00b2 / 26.67 \u2248 177.78 / 26.67 \u2248 6.67\n- Steak fries, Central: (10 - 8.00)\u00b2 / 8.00 = (2.0)\u00b2 / 8.00 = 4 / 8 = 0.50\n- Steak fries, West: (10 - 11.78)\u00b2 / 11.78 = (-1.78)\u00b2 / 11.78 \u2248 3.17 / 11.78 \u2248 0.27\n\nSumming these up:\n\u03c7\u00b2 \u2248 48.38 + 0.45 + 0.74 + 0.10 + 2.44 + 1.02 + 1.48 + 0.02 + 4.64 + 6.67 + 0.50 + 0.27\n\u03c7\u00b2 \u2248 76.75\n\n**Step 4: Determine the degrees of freedom and critical value.**\nDegrees of freedom (df) = (number o